High Templars are the psionic masters of the Protoss, wielding devastating area-of-effect spells on the battlefield. Their primary offensive ability, Psionic Storm, allows them to channel pure energy to create a roiling field of destruction, dealing heavy damage over time to all biological units caught within its area of effect, making them exceptionally effective against clustered infantry like Marines or Zerglings. Beyond raw damage, their utility is immense; they can use Hallucination to create fake copies of any Protoss unit, confusing enemies and scouting safely, or Feedback to instantly burn away all energy from a targeted caster or massive mechanical unit, often destroying them outright or leaving them powerless. This combination of overwhelming offensive power and strategic support makes them a fragile but critical component of any Protoss army, requiring careful positioning to unleash their full potential before they fall to enemy fire.
In stark contrast, Dark Templars are shadows given form, masters of stealth and surgical strikes who reject the Khala's rigid discipline. Their primary asset is their permanent invisibility, which renders them undetectable to enemies without detector units, allowing them to slip past defenses and ambush unsuspecting workers or armies. In combat, they phase into existence only to deliver devastating melee attacks with their twin warp blades, which ignore armor and can cut down most targets in just a few blows, making them exceptional for harassing mineral lines or eliminating high-value targets. Upon death, a Dark Templar can be instructed to merge with a fellow Dark Templar to form a single, more powerful Dark Archon, sacrificing its stealth for immense psionic might, capable of confusing enemy units or even taking permanent control of them. This duality of a silent, invisible assassin and the raw, chaotic power of a Dark Archon defines their role as the Protoss's tool for disruption and terror.